<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppressions for forge-works.

  ====================================================================
  KEEP IN SYNC WITH .snyk files (parallel ignore list, different format):
    .snyk                                        (root, Snyk source-of-truth)
    src/flink-jobs/pattern-matcher/.snyk         (Maven module mirror)
    src/flink-jobs/event-router/.snyk            (Maven module mirror)
    src/flink-jobs/insight-generator/.snyk       (Maven module mirror)

  When a CVE is deferred, add a matching <suppress> here AND add the
  SNYK-JAVA-* entry to all 4 .snyk files in the same commit.
  ====================================================================

  Notes on the entries below:
    - 8 are HIGH severity (CVSS 8.x). At our CRITICAL-only failure
      threshold (CVSS at or above 9) they would not fail the build even
      unsuppressed. The suppressions exist to keep the GitHub Security
      tab clean for reviewers and to maintain suppression discipline.
    - 1 is CRITICAL (CVSS 9.1) — CVE-2023-44981 in flink-shaded-zookeeper
      — WOULD fail the build unsuppressed. Kept as a time-boxed exception
      pending Flink 1.20 → 2.0 (see the per-entry <notes> for details).
    - All require Flink 1.20 → 2.0 to remediate at the source (task #24).
    - Per-CVE rationale + in-context mitigation lives in the matching
      .snyk entry (where present — DC detects some CVEs via CPE that
      Snyk's Maven index does not surface).

  Schema: https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd
  Background: AB-023 multi-scanner OSS security architecture
              (research/github_apps/multi_scanner_architecture.md).
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

