  <!-- =====================================================================
       Apache ZooKeeper (shaded inside flink-shaded-zookeeper-3, transitive
       via flink-runtime 1.20.3)
       ===================================================================== -->

  <suppress until="2026-08-10Z">
    <notes>
      CVE-2023-44981 (CVSS 9.1, CRITICAL) — Apache ZooKeeper SASL
      quorum-peer authentication bypass. Fixed in ZK 3.7.2 / 3.8.2 / 3.9.0.
      Flink 1.20.3 still ships flink-shaded-zookeeper-3 built against ZK
      3.7.1; upstream fix requires Flink 1.20 → 2.0 (task #24).

      In-context mitigation: forge-works Flink jobs run in single-node /
      HA-disabled mode within a private cluster network; the SASL quorum
      auth code path is not exposed to untrusted callers. Kept as a
      time-boxed exception at the same 2026-08-10Z review checkpoint as
      the other Flink-transitive suppressions. Do NOT extend without a
      fresh risk decision.

      Not mirrored in .snyk — Snyk's Maven index tracks
      org.apache.zookeeper:zookeeper, not org.apache.flink:flink-shaded-*,
      so this CVE is only surfaced by OWASP DC's CPE matching.
    </notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.flink/flink-shaded-zookeeper-3@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2023-44981</cve>
  </suppress>

</suppressions>
